%T A398517 3742,4409,5151,5972,6876,7867,8949,10126,11402,12781,14267,15864,
%U A398517 17576,19407,21361,23442,25654,28001,30487,33116,35892,38819,41901,45142,48546,52117,55859,59776,63872,68151,72617,77274,82126,87177,92431,97892,103564,109451
%N A398517 a(n) = (4*n^3-3*n^2+5*n+6)/6.
%C A398517 a(n) is the maximum number of regions that 3-space can be divided into by n cuts with a plane with a 90-degree fold. This is a 3-dimensional analog of A143689.
%C A398517 Dissections of three-dimensional space can be difficult to visualize, so a picture may help! Planes with a 90-degree fold are frequently encountered in rock-climbing, where they are known as "dihedrals" (see illustration).
%H A398517 Paul Williams, <a href="/A398517/a398517.jpg">Llanberis</a>, Vol. 3 of Climbers Club Guide to Wales, 1985. Illustration facing page 72. Climber (Martin Crook) on the grade E2 dihedral "German Schoolgirl", Upper Dinorwic Quarries, Llanberis, Wales. Photo: Paul Williams.
%H A398517 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-6,4,-1).
%F A398517 From _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 18 2026: (Start)
%F A398517 G.f.: (1 - 2*x + 4*x^2 + x^3)/(1 - x)^4.
%F A398517 E.g.f.: exp(x)*(6 + 6*x + 9*x^2 + 4*x^3)/6. (End)
%t A398517 a[n_] := (4*n^3 - 3*n^2 + 5*n + 6)/6; Array[a, 56, 0] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 18 2026 *)
%Y A398517 a(n) = A174723(n)+1.
%Y A398517 Cf. A000124, A000125, A130883, A143689.
%K A398517 nonn,easy,new
%O A398517 0,2
